{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZvhE9ZSwNMcqvP7xo1i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me review the findings and prepare the analysis summary:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt:11-16` — no status field yet\n- Order controller: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt:16-46` — create, get, list endpoints\n- Order repository: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderRepository.kt:11-27` — in-memory store\n- Shipment entity: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` — has `ShipmentStatus` enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- Shipment controller: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:22-56` — create, get, list endpoints\n- Shipment repository: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — in-memory store\n- Error handling: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` and `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ErrorCode enum: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` — ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository uses:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n- Error envelope structure: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n- Tests use Spring Boot test context with MockMvc for HTTP assertions\n- Tests assert both status codes AND response body structure\n- In-memory repositories with concurrent hash maps\n- Kotlin data classes for DTOs and entities\n- Pattern: create, get by id, and list endpoints\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class (required)\n2. `OrderController.kt` — add `cancel` endpoint (required)\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` — possibly add query methods to find shipments by order ID (may need if implementing in repository)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — add validation to reject creating shipments for cancelled orders (required)\n5. `ApiError.kt` — add new error codes for order cancellation (required)\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — add tests for cancel endpoint (required)\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests for shipment creation rejection when order is cancelled (required)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding status to Order changes the data structure and may break existing tests/code expecting a specific format\n- The cancellation logic needs to be atomic at the business logic level (cancel order AND cancel all its CREATED shipments together)\n- Need to handle the case where order doesn't exist\n- Need to ensure CONFIRMED shipments block cancellation entirely (no partial cancellation)\n\n**Open questions:**\n1. Should shipment queries by order ID be added to the repository, or should the repository be modified to support listing shipments by orderId? (The requirement says \"cancel every shipment of that order that is still CREATED\" so we need a way to query by orderId)\n\nLet me check if there's a method to find shipments by order ID in the repository:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` enum and update Order data class to include `status: OrderStatus` field. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderStatus.kt** (new file) — Create enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Add two new error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for attempting to create shipment for cancelled order) and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` (for attempting to cancel an order with confirmed shipments).\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Add `cancel` endpoint (`@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")`) that:\n   - Fetches the order (throws 404 if not found)\n   - If already CANCELLED, return success (idempotent)\n   - Check if any shipment for this order is CONFIRMED (throw 409 if so)\n   - Mark order as CANCELLED and all CREATED shipments as CANCELLED\n   - Return the cancelled order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Modify `create` endpoint to reject creation if the order exists and is CANCELLED (throw 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED).\n\n6. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments by order ID.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add comprehensive tests for:\n   - Cancel active order succeeds and returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel active order cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing (idempotent)\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test for:\n   - Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Instead of adding OrderStatus enum, could have used String. Rejected because enum provides type safety and consistency with ShipmentStatus pattern.\n- Could have put shipment lookup logic in the service/controller instead of repository. Rejected because repository is the data access layer and this is a query operation that belongs there.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1: Cancel an ACTIVE order with only CREATED shipments\n- Read: Order from repository, all Shipments for that order\n- Write: Update Order to CANCELLED in repository, update all CREATED Shipments to CANCELLED\n- Return: Order with status = CANCELLED, HTTP 200 OK\n\nCase 2: Cancel an already-CANCELLED order\n- Read: Order from repository\n- Write: None (idempotent)\n- Return: Order with status = CANCELLED, HTTP 200 OK\n\nCase 3: Cancel order with at least one CONFIRMED shipment\n- Read: Order, Shipments for that order\n- Write: None (transaction rolls back)\n- Return: HTTP 409 Conflict with error code (new code needed)\n\nCase 4: Cancel non-existent order\n- Read: Order not found\n- Write: None\n- Return: HTTP 404 Not Found with ORDER_NOT_FOUND error code\n\nCase 5: Create shipment for CANCELLED order\n- Read: Order from repository\n- Write: None\n- Return: HTTP 409 Conflict with new ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n- Test 1: Cancel ACTIVE order succeeds and returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n- Test 2: Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments also cancels those shipments\n- Test 3: Repeated cancel on already-CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n- Test 4: Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n- Test 5: Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\nShipmentControllerTest additions:\n- Test 1: Create shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":372,"cache_read_input_tokens":20000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":372},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2d4a6ff-2d05-4ae6-96b3-61c44d2c6dbb","uuid":"32657403-46ee-4284-a741-f76ad7d35fa4","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:18:49.879Z","request_id":"req_011CfZvhDnjQ43PKQxcXEEWc"}
